Datasets: 
overall we have 2 class of data: wilted(unhealthy) and healthy data. 
The images were collected from publicly available online sources, including platforms such as Kaggle, Pexels, and the “Plantclinic” community on Reddit. 
This approach enabled the acquisition of data that realistically reflects the diverse conditions of indoor photography, characterized by high variability in lighting, background, and composition. 
After preprocessing and annotation, the final dataset comprised 1,784 images, categorized into two classes: healthy and wilted. 
Of these, 1,428 images (80%) were used for training, and 356 images (20%) were allocated for validation. The dataset was split stratified by class to maintain a balanced distribution. 
All images were resized to 256×256 pixels, normalized, and organized according to the input requirements of the ImageDataGenerator class from the Keras library. 
The validation set remained unchanged throughout all experiments and was used consistently to evaluate model performance under equal conditions.

